[[Island]] '''Ō Shima''' ([[Japanese]]: '''大島''', '''筑前大島''') is in [[Japan]].<ref name="gn1853774"/> It is located in the prefecture of [[Fukuoka Prefecture]], in the southwestern part of the country, about {{formatnum:900}} km west of [[Tokyo (the capital city of Japan)|Tokyo]], the capital of the country. It covers an area of approximately {{formatnum:7.5}} square kilometers.
The terrain of Ō Shima is flat.{{efn|group=saysay|Calculated from elevation data (DEM 3") from Viewfinder Panoramas.<ref name="vp"/> The full algorithm is available [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Projekt_DotNetWikiBot_Framework/Lsjbot/Make-Geonames here].}} The highest point of the island is {{formatnum:206}} meters above sea level. It spans 3.1 km from north to south and 4.0 km from east to west.{{efn|group=saysay|Calculated from elevation data (DEM 3") from Viewfinder Panoramas.<ref name="vp"/> The full algorithm is available [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Projekt_DotNetWikiBot_Framework/Lsjbot/Make-Geonames here].}}
The climate is [[temperate]]. The average temperature is {{formatnum:15}} [[°C]]. The warmest month is August, at {{formatnum:24}}&nbsp;[[°C]], and the coldest is February, at {{formatnum:6}}&nbsp;°C.<ref name="nasa"/> The average annual rainfall is {{formatnum:2130}} millimeters. The wettest month is July, with {{formatnum:410}} millimeters of rain, and the driest is January, with {{formatnum:47}} millimeters.<ref name="nasarain"/>
{| class="climate chart" |- | '''Ō Shima Climate Data''' | January | 5 | 8 | 47 | February | 4 | 7 | 157 | March | 6 | 13 | 136 | April | 10 | 17 | 120 | May | 14 | 20 | 89 | June | 15 | 21 | 294 | July | 20 | 22 | 410 | August | 23 | 26 | 383 | September | 19 | 21 | 146 | October | 17 | 21 | 126 | November | 12 | 16 | 124 | December | 7 | 11 | 98 |- | Data source: <ref name="nasa"/> |}
